# Process topology for the VerseID backend. `web` is the only one that
# serves HTTP traffic; `worker` and `beat` run background/scheduled jobs
# (see config/celery.py) and need a Redis instance reachable via REDIS_URL.
#
# Deploy `beat` as EXACTLY ONE instance — it's the thing that decides when
# charge_renewals / send_daily_verse run, and more than one running at once
# means they'd fire multiple times on the same schedule (the same bug this
# whole setup replaces — see config/celery.py's docstring). `web` and
# `worker` can each be scaled to more than one instance freely.
web: gunicorn config.wsgi:application
worker: celery -A config worker --loglevel=info --concurrency=2
beat: celery -A config beat --loglevel=info